CODEGEN.md §3.3, §3.5, decision 194: an enum member's @go(name:) is its whole constant, so ToneB on member a collides with member b's own ToneB in the package scope.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tone.
enum Tone { a @go(name: "ToneB"), b }

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:4:35
  go: ToneB is generated for both a.Tone.a and a.Tone.b

